<main id="main-content" class="founder-page">
  <section class="founder-section" aria-labelledby="founder-building">
    <div class="founder-wrap founder-split">
      <div><p class="founder-eyebrow">Who We Are</p><h2 id="founder-building">Built on experience.<br>Driven by perspective.</h2><p>Minimalism LLC was founded around a simple principle: Signal Over Noise.</p><p>Signal Audit puts that principle to work. It receives operational signals, evaluates their significance, and helps teams understand where to look next.</p><p>Our ambition is not to create another place to watch alerts. It is to make the information organizations already have more useful for the decisions they need to make.</p></div>
      <figure><img src="/assets/images/founder-pitch.png" alt="Kwansah Madani speaking into a microphone at a founder pitch event" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Building and sharing the vision for Signal Audit.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="founder-hero" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
    <div class="founder-wrap founder-hero-grid">
      <div class="founder-hero-copy">
        <!--<p class="founder-eyebrow">Who We Are</p>
        <h1 id="founder-title">Built on experience.<br>Driven by perspective.</h1>-->
        <p class="founder-lede">Signal Audit is built on a belief that operational data should lead to understanding, not just more noise.</p>
        <p>We turn signals from complex production environments into clearer evidence, priorities, and next steps.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="founder-portrait"><img src="/assets/images/founder-portrait.jpg" alt="Kwansah Madani at a Tri-Valley Life Sciences event" width="1488" height="992"><figcaption>Kwansah Madani · Founder, Minimalism LLC &amp; Signal Audit</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="founder-section" aria-labelledby="founder-person">
    <div class="founder-wrap founder-copy">
      <p class="founder-eyebrow">Meet the founder</p>
      <h2 id="founder-person">A career spent making complex systems understandable.</h2>
      <p>Kwansah Madani brings nearly two decades of experience across front-end engineering, product optimization, site reliability, and observability. His work has included enterprise environments at Wells Fargo, Williams-Sonoma, and MTV.</p>
      <p>Across those settings, one pattern kept appearing: teams could collect extraordinary amounts of telemetry and still struggle to decide what deserved attention. The challenge was not simply seeing more. It was knowing what mattered.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="founder-section founder-section-alt" aria-labelledby="founder-thinking">
    <div class="founder-wrap founder-split">
      <div><p class="founder-eyebrow">The perspective</p><h2 id="founder-thinking">Observability is a starting point. Judgment is the work.</h2><p>Dashboards, alerts, and AI-generated summaries can all be useful. But operational intelligence requires evidence, context, accountability, and a clear path to action.</p><p>Signal Audit is designed to help teams interpret what their systems are telling them—without pretending that software should replace the people responsible for those systems.</p></div>
      <figure><img src="/assets/images/founder-speaking.png" alt="Kwansah Madani speaking onstage at a technology event" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Sharing ideas with the technology community.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="founder-section" aria-labelledby="founder-building">
    <div class="founder-wrap founder-split">
      <figure><img src="/assets/images/founder-pitch.png" alt="Kwansah Madani speaking into a microphone at a founder pitch event" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Building and sharing the vision for Signal Audit.</figcaption></figure>
      <div><p class="founder-eyebrow">Why we built it</p><h2 id="founder-building">From production experience to a product with a point of view.</h2><p>Minimalism LLC was founded around a simple principle: Signal Over Noise.</p><p>Signal Audit puts that principle to work. It receives operational signals, evaluates their significance, and helps teams understand where to look next.</p><p>Our ambition is not to create another place to watch alerts. It is to make the information organizations already have more useful for the decisions they need to make.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="founder-closing" aria-labelledby="founder-close"><div class="founder-wrap"><p class="founder-eyebrow">Our philosophy</p><h2 id="founder-close">Signal Over Noise.<br>Know What Matters.</h2><p>Explore the thinking, the evidence, and the company behind Signal Audit.</p><div class="founder-actions"><a href="/case-studies">Case Studies</a><a href="/whitepapers">Research &amp; Whitepapers</a><a href="https://minimalism.agency/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Minimalism LLC</a></div></div></section>
</main>
